	<!--  HOW IT WORKS                                                           -->
	<!-- ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════ -->
	<div class="ix-flow-section section" id="how-it-works">
		<div class="container">
			<div class="section-header" style="margin-bottom:0">
				<div class="section-eyebrow">Architecture</div>
				<h2 class="section-title">
					How Inbox <em>works</em>
				</h2>
				<p class="section-sub">
					Five Cloudflare primitives working together — no external infrastructure, no servers to manage.
				</p>
			</div>

			<div class="ix-flow-wrap">
				<div class="ix-flow-step">
					<div class="ix-flow-tag ix-tag-routing">Cloudflare</div>
					<div class="ix-flow-num">1</div>
					<h4>Email Routing</h4>
					<p>
						Configure a catch-all or address-specific rule in your Cloudflare dashboard to forward inbound
						mail to the inbox Worker.
					</p>
				</div>
				<div class="ix-flow-step">
					<div class="ix-flow-tag ix-tag-worker">Worker</div>
					<div class="ix-flow-num">2</div>
					<h4>email() handler</h4>
					<p>
						The inbox Worker's <code style="font-size:11px">email()</code> handler fires for every inbound
						message. It parses MIME, stores the raw email and attachments in R2, and writes the contact +
						thread row to D1.
					</p>
				</div>
				<div class="ix-flow-step">
					<div class="ix-flow-tag ix-tag-db">D1 + R2</div>
					<div class="ix-flow-num">3</div>
					<h4>Contacts &amp; threads</h4>
					<p>
						D1 holds contacts, email metadata, users, inboxes, and sequence schedules. R2 stores raw email
						bodies and attachments with secure per-request signed URLs.
					</p>
				</div>
				<div class="ix-flow-step">
					<div class="ix-flow-tag ix-tag-dash">Dashboard</div>
					<div class="ix-flow-num">4</div>
					<h4>Inbox UI + Push</h4>
					<p>
						The React dashboard SPA is served directly from the Worker's Assets binding. On new email, a
						Durable Object fans out a WebSocket notification to all open sessions.
					</p>
				</div>
				<div class="ix-flow-step">
					<div class="ix-flow-tag ix-tag-queue">Queues + Cron</div>
					<div class="ix-flow-num">5</div>
					<h4>Sequences</h4>
					<p>
						A cron trigger runs every 5 minutes to enqueue due sequence steps. The queue consumer sends
						replies via the CF Email Sending API with deduplication and retry logic.
					</p>
				</div>
			</div>
		</div>
	</div>

