				<!-- UPGRADING -->
				<section class="doc-section" id="upgrading">
					<div class="doc-section-header">
						<h2>Upgrading</h2>
						<a class="anchor-link" href="#upgrading">
							#upgrading
						</a>
					</div>
					<div class="doc-body">
						<p>
							Pull the latest code and re-deploy. The <code>dashboard-deploy</code> just recipe runs
							remote D1 migrations before deploying so schema changes are applied atomically.
						</p>

						<pre class="code-block"><code><span class="cb-cmt"># Pull latest</span>
<span class="cb-cmd">git pull origin trunk</span>
<span class="cb-cmd">just install</span>

<span class="cb-cmt"># Apply any new migrations + rebuild + redeploy</span>
<span class="cb-cmd">just dashboard-deploy</span></code></pre>

						<h3>
							What <code>just dashboard-deploy</code> does
						</h3>
						<ul>
							<li>
								Runs <code>wrangler d1 migrations apply DB --remote</code> to apply pending SQL
								migrations to the live database.
							</li>
							<li>Builds the Next.js app with React Server Components and Server Actions.</li>
							<li>
								Deploys the single unified Worker bundle with Hono API and Durable Objects to
								Cloudflare.
							</li>
						</ul>

						<div class="callout callout-green">
							<span class="callout-icon">✅</span>
							<span>
								Migrations are idempotent — already-applied migrations are skipped automatically. You
								can safely run <code>just dashboard-deploy</code> at any time without risk of data loss.
							</span>
						</div>
					</div>
				</section>
			</main>
		</div>
